bility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kangra Airport, Gaggal","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.8,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nagrota railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Shri Chamunda Devi Mandir), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"0a4e1758-5f70-4392-bcb5-e30de205c108","name":"Mata Mansa Devi Mandir, Panchkula","deity":"Mansa Devi — a form of Shakti also invoked for protection from snakebite","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Haryana","district":"Panchkula","town":"Panchkula","latitude":30.76528,"longitude":76.82694,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Jhajra nadi River","river_distance_km":6.1,"best_season_notes":"Navratri in both Chaitra (Mar–Apr) and Ashvin (Sep–Oct) are the major fairs, each drawing very large crowds daily.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T19:09:34.948917+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Local tradition holds this is one of the sites where a part of Sati fell (a \"Shakti Peetha\" in the loose, non-canonical sense some regional sources use — it is not on the standard scholarly 51-site list, so is not tagged as such here). The documented, verifiable history is more recent: the present main temple was built by Maharaja Gopal Singh of Manimajra between 1811 and 1815, with a subsidiary shrine (the Patiala Shivalaya, containing painted wall panels dated 1870 Vikram Samvat) added around 1840. The Haryana government constituted the Shri Mata Mansa Devi Shrine Board to administer the complex in 1991.","etiquette_notes":"A roughly 100-acre complex at the foot of the Shivalik hills with several sub-shrines alongside the main temple — expect very long queues during Navratri.","native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Summer roughly 4am–10pm, winter roughly 5am–9pm; aartis around 5am and 6am.","accessibility_notes":"A large, mostly flat paved complex; some sub-shrines within the grounds involve short flights of steps, but unlike Naina Devi or Chandi Devi the main approach is not a hill-climb.","nearest_airport_name":"Chandigarh Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":17,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chandigarh Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia; Haryana Tourism","architecture_style":"North Indian temple architecture","construction_century":19},{"id":"0a7c8dd2-4c38-42f4-8c86-354356a0ba5d","name":"Sree Vallabha Temple, Thiruvalla","deity":"Vallabha (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Malai Nadu Divya Desam"],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Pathanamthitta","town":"Thiruvalla","latitude":9.3833,"longitude":76.5667,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Manimala","river_distance_km":0.3,"best_season_notes":"Feb–Mar for the temple's annual festival; otherwise Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:20:34.20482+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A roughly 400-year-old temple on the banks of the Manimala river, with the deity's installation traditionally dated far earlier. Known for its 54-foot Garuda Sthambham, a flagstaff carved from a single block of granite, and unusual for being one of the very few temples anywhere that offers Kathakali as a regular nightly ritual to the deity, performed after the evening pooja.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"തിരുവല്ല ശ്രീവല്ലഭക്ഷേത്രം","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Cochin International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":87.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Thiruvalla railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"0b423b1e-d1fa-47ec-b4d3-4244a1e4f723","name":"Bhawani Waghjai Temple, Terav","deity":"Bhawani and Waghjai","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Maharashtra","district":"Ratnagiri","town":"Chiplun","latitude":17.47852,"longitude":73.53724,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vashishti River","river_distance_km":5.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in Terav village, Chiplun taluka, Ratnagiri, whose original building dates to around 1860. It houses the goddesses Bhawani, Waghjai, Kalkai and Navdurga along with Shiva. The hall measures about 123 ft long, and the state has listed it as a tourist place.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Ratnagiri Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":56.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Kamathe railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.