ndly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Chenjiyaru River","river_distance_km":1.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple at Villianur in Puducherry where Shiva is worshipped as a lingam and his consort as Kokilambigai. The two-acre complex has shrines enclosed by concentric rectangular walls. The original is believed to be Chola work with later additions, and the Puducherry government's HR&CE department now administers it.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Puducherry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":8.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Chinnababu Samudram railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Kameeswarar temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Chola with later additions","construction_century":null},{"id":"144b9db3-7cb1-4166-9dc7-ddb0d48a9cc7","name":"Modhera Sun Temple","deity":"Surya","sampradaya":"Saura","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Gujarat","district":"Mehsana","town":"Modhera","latitude":23.5866,"longitude":72.1316,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Pushpavati River","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Feb; the temple is aligned so the equinox sunrise lines up with the sanctum.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T13:57:28.972216+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built in 1026–27 CE by the Solanki king Bhima I, shortly after defending Gujarat from Mahmud of Ghazni's raid on the Somnath temple — the Solankis, who traced their lineage to the sun god Surya, built it partly as a political statement of that dynasty's own resilience. The complex is precisely oriented so that the sun at the equinoxes shines directly through the hall into the sanctum. A separate tradition holds Rama and Sita rested here on their return from Lanka, and the Bhavishya Purana ties the town's name to a blind Brahmin, Modha, healed here by Surya's grace.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"મોઢેરા સૂર્ય મંદિર","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":76.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khambel railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":9.4,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition, referencing the Bhavishya Purana","architecture_style":"Maru-Gurjara","construction_century":11},{"id":"1474c09e-8730-4c12-b3cd-de5c7858e8e5","name":"Baleshwar Temple","deity":"Shiva as Baleshwar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Champawat","town":"Chouki","latitude":29.3366,"longitude":80.0904,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Lohaghat Nadi River","river_distance_km":4.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:20.030396+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"An old Shiva temple in Champawat, Uttarakhand, built by the Chand rulers and noted for its stone carving. It is thought to date to 1390, with reconstruction begun by Uday Chand around 1420-21 and completed by Hari Chand, as a copperplate inscription of 1423 records.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pantnagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":68.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tanakpur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":30,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Baleshwar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Stone-carved (Chand dynasty)","construction_century":14},{"id":"147a8c1e-c0c5-4588-91f2-cc058d75fcc3","name":"Kandariya Mahadev Temple, Khajuraho","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Chhatarpur","town":"Khajuraho","latitude":24.8318,"longitude":79.9199,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khudar River","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Oct–Mar; part of the Khajuraho Group of Monuments (UNESCO), known for its temple architecture.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Built under the Chandela dynasty in the 11th century, this is the largest of the surviving Khajuraho temples — part of a group originally numbering around 85 shrines, of which about 25 survive. Its elaborate exterior carvings, covering every register of human experience, are traditionally read as a teaching on the passage from worldly desire (kama) toward liberation (moksha), with the sanctum housed at the end of a long ascent representing that same journey.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"कंदारिया महादेव मन्दिर","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Khajuraho Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khajuraho Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Nagara","construction_century":11},{"id":"1488650c-34f2-42b0-8147-d1e17e3b241f","name":"Bijasan Mata Temple, Salkanpur","deity":"Vindhyavasini Bijasan Devi (Durga)","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Sehore","town":"Salkanpur","latitude":22.74517,"longitude":77.47994,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Narmada River","river_distance_km":9.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Siddhpeeth of Vindhyavasini Beejasan Devi, regarded as a form of Durga, on an 800-foot hill at Salkanpur, about 70 km from Bhopal. Roughly 1400 steps lead to the summit, and the temple is considered one of the holiest for Hindus.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Raja Bhoj Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":