 one of the six Arupadaiveedu (Six Abodes of Murugan) situated directly on the seashore.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"திருச்செந்தூர் முருகன் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"General daily hours around 5am–9pm (paid-darshan queue closes 6:30pm, general queue 7pm), with extended hours during festivals — per a recent news report, not an official schedule.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin (Thoothukudi) Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":27,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Tiruchendur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":0,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Subramaniya Swamy Temple, Tiruchendur)","architecture_style":"Dravidian, built largely of red sandstone; unusually for a Dravidian temple, its nine-tier Raja Gopuram (about 157 ft/48 m high) faces west rather than east","construction_century":null},{"id":"1626b9cc-ff41-4747-a72f-ac16016f03dd","name":"Bucesvara Temple, Koravangala","deity":"Shiva and Surya","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Hassan","town":"Chikkabuvanahalli","latitude":13.05331,"longitude":76.17706,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A 12th-century Hoysala twin temple in Koravangala village, built by a wealthy patron named Buchi in the reign of King Ballala. One sanctum faces east and honours Shiva; the other, near the entrances, honours Surya. Carvings include Shaiva, Vaishnava and Shakta art