It lies 15 km from the city and 37 km from Jolly Grant Airport.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Dehradun Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":27.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Dehradun railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":9.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Santala devi temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"1717f4ea-2c9a-43d9-a454-452c7982aed9","name":"Srivilliputhur Andal Temple","deity":"Andal / Vatapatrasayi (Vishnu)","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Virudhunagar","town":"Srivilliputhur","latitude":9.5136,"longitude":77.6328,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Jan for Margazhi, when Andal's Thiruppavai verses are recited daily — this also happens to sit right after Tamil Nadu's northeast-monsoon rains (heaviest Oct–Nov) have cleared, so it is a genuinely good time to travel, not just a festival window.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T20:39:31.59741+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"The birthplace of Andal, the only woman among the twelve Alvar poet-saints, who by tradition wore garlands intended for the deity before offering them and was ultimately taken in marriage by Vishnu at Srirangam. One of the 108 Divya Desams.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"ஸ்ரீவில்லிபுத்தூர் ஆண்டாள் கோயில்","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Madurai International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":61.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Srivilliputtur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":2.2,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Naalayira Divya Prabandham (Alvar hymn tradition)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"17483762-ccc0-47a3-b05c-59ff4f6ab5a6","name":"Chennamangalam Temple","deity":"Ayyappa","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Kozhikode","town":"Chorode","latitude":11.6208,"longitude":75.5849,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"vykkilaseri padavathumthazhe River","river_distance_km":0.4,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:56.940052+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple in Chorode, Kozhikode district, where Ayyappa is the main deity, with Shiva, Ganesha, Vishnu and Annapurneshwari also worshipped. It is called a second Sabarimala and is regarded as one of Kerala's older temples. Its roof was renovated with teak in 2018, and the annual utsav, usually in April, favours traditional arts.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kannur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":33.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vadakara railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Chennamangalam Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"17486ad0-9d1d-4ff7-b206-65c8c0367923","name":"Andhra Maha Vishnu Temple, Srikakulam (Krishna district)","deity":"Vishnu (Andhra Maha Vishnu) / Rajya Lakshmi Devi","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["Divya Desam"],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Krishna","town":"Srikakulam","latitude":16.2,"longitude":80.85,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Krishna","river_distance_km":0.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:36:33.433509+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"Counted as the 57th of the 108 Divya Desams. The temple bears 32 inscriptions, including ones from the Vijayanagara emperor Krishnadevaraya, who is recorded to have visited during his Kalinga campaign around 1515–1516 CE and is traditionally said to have composed the opening verses of his Telugu work Amuktamalyada here. A popular sthala purana, recounted in the Andhra Kaumudi, describes \"Andhra Vishnu\" building a wall linking Srisailam, Bhimeswaram and Kaleswaram with three gates for three lingams, after which the region came to be called \"Trilingam\" — a traditional account offered as the origin of the name \"Andhra\", not an established historical or linguistic fact. Note: this village, in Krishna district's Ghantasala mandal on the bank of the Krishna river, is distinct from Srikakulam town/district in north coastal Andhra Pradesh.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Vijayawada Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":36.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Vemuru railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":11.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Andhra Kaumudi (traditional account); temple inscriptions","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"17af0820-25b8-419f-a982-bca0d2bf9974","name":"Dadhimati Mata Temple","deity":"Dadhimati Mata","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Nagaur","town":"Tejasar","latitude":27.2373,"longitude":74.0755,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":null,"river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple of the goddess Dadhimati in Nagaur district, Rajasthan, with an inscription suggesting it existed by 608 CE. She is the family deity of Dahima communities and the temple is counted among the 52 Shakti peethas. Large fairs are held twice a year during Navratri. Tradition regards her as sister of the sage Dadhichi.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kishangarh Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":102.5,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khatu railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":28.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Dadhimati Mata Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":7},{"id":"17f3eb56-f54f-4a04-a2df-b616d11a7f3d","name":"ISKCON Sri Sri Radha Madhava Temple, Mayapur","deity":"Radha-Madhava (Radha and Krishna) with the Ashta-sakhis, worshipped today in the existing Chandrodaya Mandir complex; the site also has separate altars for the Pancha-tattva (Chaitanya Mahaprabhu and associates) and Narasimhadeva. A much larger building, the Temple of the Vedic Planetarium, is under construction nearby and not yet open.","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":["ISKCON headquarters complex"],"country":"India","state":"West Bengal","district":"Nadia","town":"Mayapur","latitude":23.4249,"longitude":88.3892,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Ganges (at its confluence with the Jalangi)","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":"Gaura Purnima (Chaitanya Mahaprabhu's appearance day) is the major festival, marked by a multi-day Navadvipa-mandala parikrama; Chandan Yatra, Ratha Yatra and Radhashtami are also observed.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T09:14:22.726852+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-22T09:14:22.726852+00:00","sthala_purana":"Identified by Bhaktivinoda Thakur in 1894 as the birthplace of Chaitanya Mahaprabhu — a matter of religious tradition and identification, not archaeological certainty. Founded by A. C. Bhaktivedanta Swami Prabhupada as a planned pilgrimage site and headquarters for ISKCON; construction of the Temple of the Vedic Planetarium began in 2009 and is scheduled to open in 2027, after which it is intended to be the largest religious monument in the world.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":"Darshan is commonly cited as roughly 7am–12:30pm and 4–8pm, with a detailed daily aarti schedule (mangala arati around 4:30am through sandhya arati around 6:30pm) — sourced from third-party tourism aggregators rather than the temple's own published schedule, so treat as approximate.","accessibility_notes":"ISKCON operates on-campus guesthouses for pilgrims; reachable by road and by rail via Nabadwip Dham railway station.","nearest_airport_name":"Netaji Subhas Chandra Bose International Airport, Kolkata","nearest_airport_distance_km":110,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nabadwip Dham railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":null,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Bhaktivinoda Thakur (1894 identification); ISKCON/Mayapur project records","architecture_style":"The planned Temple of the Vedic Planetarium is a large blue-domed structure incorporating Vedic cosmological elements — a representation of Mount Meru and a \"universal chandelier\" — blending temple form with planetarium functionality; still under construction.","construction_century":null},{"id":"1901cf0a-5521-444b-abbc-290d7330ed80","name":"Manakula Vinayagar Temple","deity":"Ganesha as Vinayagar","sampradaya":"Ganapatya","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Puducherry","district":"Puducherry","town":"Puducherry","latitude":11.93583,"longitude":79.83361,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Chenjiyaru River","river_distance_km":6.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:44.755986+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Ganesha temple in Puducherry that is both a popular pilgrimage site and a tourist attraction. It is considered very old and pre-dates French rule. The article says attempts to destroy it during Dupleix's time were stopped by strong Hindu protests and by fear of British and Maratha attacks.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Puducherry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":4.3,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Puducherry railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":1.3,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Manakula Vinayagar Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"1920ee97-0cc7-454e-b10a-3d3c64213863","name":"Parassinikadavu Muthappan Temple","deity":"Muthappan (Vishnu-Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Kerala","district":"Kannur","town":"Parassinikadavu","latitude":11.9667,"longitude":75.4167,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Valapattanam","river_distance_km":0.2,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Jan for the Puthari Thiruvappana festival; otherwise Oct–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-04T18:27:49.795249+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A markedly non-traditional temple: worship here centres on the daily Theyyam ritual rather than fixed-idol puja, is open to devotees of every caste and religion, and offers fish, toddy, and meat as prasadam. Local tradition holds Muthappan was a divine child found by a childless couple on the riverbank, whose unconventional habits led to his being cast out, after which he was revealed to combine the forms of Vishnu (as Thiruvappana) and Shiva (as Vellattom). Dogs are considered sacred here as Muthappan’s companions and roam the temple freely.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":"പറശ്ശിനിക്കടവ് മുത്തപ്പൻ ക്ഷേത്രം","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kannur International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.9,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Pappinisseri railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":8.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"1922ce6b-5d81-4c3a-b3e9-2542e2ad87e7","name":"Pathrol Kali Temple, Madhupur","deity":"Kali","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Jharkhand","district":"Deoghar","town":"Karon","latitude":24.24472,"longitude":86.70194,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Puthro River","river_distance_km":3,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:05:32.681015+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A shrine to Kali about 7 km from Madhupur in Deoghar, built by Raja Digvijay Singh some six to seven centuries ago. Worship is held daily and animals are sacrificed. Nine more temples stand nearby, and a large annual fair takes place in the month of Kartik.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Deoghar International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":22.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Joramow railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Pathrol Kali Temple, Madhupur), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"19244deb-1e25-41eb-913e-8e2d6f1528eb","name":"Matangeshvara Temple, Khajuraho","deity":"Shiva as Matangeshvara","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Madhya Pradesh","district":"Chhatarpur","town":"Khajuraho","latitude":24.85193,"longitude":79.92169,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khudar River","river_distance_km":1.8,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:47.875457+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple in Khajuraho, Madhya Pradesh, and the only Chandela-era monument there still in active worship. It belongs to the Khajuraho Group of Monuments, which was inscribed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1986 for its art and architecture.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Khajuraho Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":4.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Khajuraho railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Matangeshvara Temple, Khajuraho), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Chandela","construction_century":null},{"id":"1969a053-3350-4e5d-9043-31dc6f11c6df","name":"Bhand Deva Temple","deity":"Shiva","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Rajasthan","district":"Baran","town":"Ramgarh","latitude":25.33333,"longitude":76.62417,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Khul River","river_distance_km":2.1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T10:59:23.880063+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A temple complex near Ramgarh in Baran district, Rajasthan, on the shore of a crater lake. The main Shiva temple, in Nagara style with Khajuraho-like sculpture, is described on a site plaque as 10th-century and Tantric Shaiva. Over 750 steps lead up to cave shrines of the goddesses Kisnai and Annapurna, where a fair is held at Kartik Purnima.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kota Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":80.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Baran railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":29,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Bhand Deva Temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Nagara","construction_century":10},{"id":"19c63c54-c9df-4a2b-a867-97a8a29add01","name":"Perur Pateeswarar Temple, Coimbatore","deity":"Shiva as Pateeswarar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Coimbatore","town":"Perur","latitude":10.97583,"longitude":76.91472,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Noyyal","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:38:59.708182+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Shiva temple at Perur in western Coimbatore, on the bank of the Noyyal River, said to have been built by Karikala Chola in the 2nd century CE. Pateeswarar, a self-manifested lingam, is worshipped with his consort Pachainayaki. Poets such as Arunagirinathar and Kachiappa Munivar patronised it, and it has been known by many names including Melai Chidambaram.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Coimbatore International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":15.7,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Coimbatore North railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Perur Pateeswarar Temple, Coimbatore), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":2},{"id":"19e44a74-f0e5-4409-98a0-5c544bd8a431","name":"Tirupacchur Vaccheeswarar Temple, Tiruvallur","deity":"Vaccheeswarar (Shiva)","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Tiruvallur","town":"Tirupacchur, Tiruvallur","latitude":13.165,"longitude":79.895,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Kosasthalaiyar River","river_distance_km":5,"best_season_notes":"Nov–Feb.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-08T06:51:40.218447+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Reported to be around 1,500 years old, a Shiva temple at Tirupacchur village near Tiruvallur.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airpor