n","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Mahanadi","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":"Rajim Kumbh (the fair at the Triveni Sangam of the Mahanadi, Pairi and Sondur rivers) draws the biggest crowds; sources disagree on whether it falls at Magh Purnima or Maha Shivaratri.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:05:50.919949+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-26T20:05:50.919949+00:00","sthala_purana":"Dating is contested: an inscription attributes the temple to Vilasatunga of the Nala dynasty, placed in the 8th century on the style of the script, while others, following Cunningham, argue for a 5th-century origin with the inscription recording a restoration. Legends variously credit Vishvakarma, or a king called Jagat Pal who is said to have finished it in a day, or King Ratnakar after a vision. The complex also stands near the Kuleshwar Mahadev temple.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Swami Vivekananda Airport, Raipur","nearest_airport_distance_km":42,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Raipur Junction","nearest_railway_distance_km":50,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Gariaband district site; Wikipedia (Rajiv Lochan Temple)","architecture_style":"Pancayatana plan with four corner shrines (Narasimha, Vamana, Varaha, Badrinatha) and a sanctum tower of about 50 ft","construction_century":null},{"id":"1a3c2a72-f9e0-4e28-8879-ebe974b5215e","name":"Shri Raghunath Mandir","deity":"Rama","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Himachal Pradesh","district":"Kullu","town":"Kullu","latitude":31.96099,"longitude":77.11383,