":null,"native_name":"கைலாசநாதர் கோயில், தென்திருப்பேரை","morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Tuticorin Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":14.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Nazareth railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":4.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Local/regional tradition (Agastya-Romasa Muni legend)","architecture_style":"Dravidian","construction_century":null},{"id":"1eb47971-788d-47b1-b689-8d016ea5bd62","name":"Lingaraj Temple, Bhubaneswar","deity":"Shiva-Vishnu (Harihara/Lingaraja)","sampradaya":null,"significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Odisha","district":"Khordha","town":"Bhubaneswar","latitude":20.2373,"longitude":85.8344,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Bindusagar (temple tank)","river_distance_km":0.1,"best_season_notes":"Dec–Feb; non-Hindus are traditionally not permitted inside, viewing platform available outside. Bhubaneswar is a little inland of the coast, so it sees less direct cyclone exposure than Puri or Konark, but the same winter window is most comfortable.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T11:51:56.898831+00:00","updated_at":"2026-09-05T18:23:31.36475+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of Odisha's oldest and largest temples, with a documented history stretching back over a thousand years under successive Somavamshi and Ganga dynasty patronage. The presiding deity, Harihara, combines Shiva and Vishnu in a single form, and the temple compound is described at length in the Ekamra Purana, a regional Sanskrit text devoted to the sacred geography of Bhubaneswar.","etiquette_notes":"Only Hindus are traditionally permitted inside the main sanctum; a viewing platform outside is provided for others.","native_name":"ଲିଙ୍ଗରାଜ ମନ୍ଦିର","morning_opens_at":"06:00:00","morning_closes_at":"12:30:00","evening_opens_at":"15:30:00","evening_closes_at":"21:00:00","timings_notes":"Extended to roughly 3:30am–11pm during Maha Shivratri.","accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Biju Patnaik International Airport, Bhubaneswar","nearest_airport_distance_km":2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhubaneswar Railway Station","nearest_railway_distance_km":6,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":null,"architecture_style":"Kalinga","construction_century":11},{"id":"1eb5a79c-6b4c-43b9-b5df-8240c9d29329","name":"Baijnath Temple Complex","deity":"Shiva as Vaidyanath, with Parvati","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Uttarakhand","district":"Bageshwar","town":"Baijnāth","latitude":29.92,"longitude":79.625,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Gomati","river_distance_km":null,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:11.054915+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-04T12:15:48.914317+00:00","sthala_purana":"A cluster of 18 stone temples on the left bank of the Gomati river in Baijnath, at about 1,125 m. It is noted for a depiction of Parvati together with Shiva. The principal deities include Vaidyanath, Parvati, Nritya Ganapati, Karttikeya, Narasimha, Brahma and Surya. Pilgrims gather at Shivratri and Makar Sankranti.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Pantnagar Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":9