samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Sakri River","river_distance_km":1.8,"best_season_notes":"The month-long Shravani Mela (Jul–Aug) and Maha Shivaratri (Feb–Mar) are the major seasons.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-22T08:39:44.697229+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"One of three major Shiva temples of the Bihar–Jharkhand region, alongside Baidyanath Temple at Deoghar and Ajgaibinath Temple. Basukinath is traditionally the second leg of the Kanwar/Shravani pilgrimage: devotees first offer jal at Baidyanath Dham, Deoghar, then travel roughly 45 km here to complete the ritual. The 30-shrine complex is built in Nagara style with a pyramid-shaped shikhara; an exact founding century is not reliably documented.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Deoghar International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":51.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Poreyahat railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":3.5,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia; regional pilgrimage tradition","architecture_style":"Nagara style, pyramid-shaped shikhara","construction_century":null},{"id":"1fc8674f-c03a-44e5-9310-ece8abdfa03e","name":"Betrayaswamy temple","deity":"Vishnu as Devaperumal","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Tamil Nadu","district":"Krishnagiri","town":"Denkanikottai","latitude":12.51611,"longitude":77.79861,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Chinnar River","river_distance_km":8.5,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:38.937899+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A Vishnu temple in Denkanikottai, built in Hoysala style, with Lakshmi as Soundaryavalli. The Wodeyars of Mysore added pillared halls and major shrines in the 16th century. A granite wall and five-tiered gopuram mark it. It follows the Tenkalai tradition, and the Chittirai Kalyana Utsavam is a main festival.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Kempegowda International Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":76.4,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Periyanaga Thunai railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":13.1,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Betrayaswamy temple), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":"Hoysala","construction_century":16},{"id":"1fe14133-8bd1-4b4f-9de9-6a764193d139","name":"Lakshmi Narasimha Swamy Temple, Antarvedi","deity":"Lakshmi Narasimha, with Rajyalakshmi","sampradaya":"Vaishnava","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Andhra Pradesh","district":"Dr. B. R. Ambedkar Konaseema","town":"Antarvedi","latitude":16.3333,"longitude":81.7333,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Vasishta Godavari River","river_distance_km":1.2,"best_season_notes":"The Kalyanotsavam falls in the month of Magha, beginning around Ratha Saptami, with the Lord's wedding on Magha Shukla Dashami; Narasimha Jayanti in Vaisakha is also observed.","submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-09-26T20:40:38.920003+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"Tradition says the sage Vasishta founded an ashram here after bringing a branch of the Godavari to the sea, that Brahma installed the deity, that Narasimha fought the demon Raktavilochana (giving the Raktakulya river its name), and that a cowherd named Kesavadas rediscovered the temple in the Kali Yuga. The temple's construction dates conflict: Wikipedia credits Kopanathi Krishnamma with completing it in Saka 1745 (1823 CE), while the district site records a major reconstruction in 1923 — neither is stated as fact here. Coordinates are village-level.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Rajahmundry Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":86.2,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Narasapur railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":12.8,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"East Godavari district site; Wikipedia (Lakshmi Narasimha Temple, Antarvedi)","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":null},{"id":"20478a05-01c7-4a22-8696-903bf3efc9be","name":"Chitrapur Math","deity":"Shiva as Bhavanishankar","sampradaya":"Shaiva","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Karnataka","district":"Uttara Kannada","town":"Shirali","latitude":14.03107,"longitude":74.53487,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Venkatapura River","river_distance_km":1,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:03:52.882408+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"The central math of the Chitrapur Saraswat Brahmin community, at Shirali in Uttara Kannada since 1757. Its presiding deity is Bhavanishankar, a form of Shiva, and six other sanctums hold the samadhis of earlier gurus. Daily puja is offered at these shrines, and the current seer is the eleventh of a lineage begun in 1708.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"evening_closes_at":null,"timings_notes":null,"accessibility_notes":null,"nearest_airport_name":"Shivamogga Airport","nearest_airport_distance_km":118.6,"nearest_railway_station_name":"Bhatkal railway station","nearest_railway_distance_km":5.7,"emergency_contact_notes":null,"sthala_purana_source":"Wikipedia (Chitrapur Math), summarised; location via OpenStreetMap","architecture_style":null,"construction_century":18},{"id":"2063b236-c391-4be7-9ba5-f3c60045bb77","name":"Aranya Devi Temple, Arrah","deity":"Aranya Devi","sampradaya":"Shakta","significance":[],"country":"India","state":"Bihar","district":"Bhojpur","town":"Jamira","latitude":25.5679,"longitude":84.67299,"sandhya_friendly":"unknown","sandhya_notes":null,"samidhadhanam_friendly":"unknown","samidhadhanam_notes":null,"food_tier":"unknown","food_source_name":null,"food_source_contact":null,"food_distance_km":null,"nearest_river_name":"Son River","river_distance_km":10.2,"best_season_notes":null,"submitted_by":null,"status":"approved","verified_by":null,"moderator_note":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T11:04:54.58588+00:00","updated_at":"2026-11-05T02:38:03.965515+00:00","sthala_purana":"A goddess temple in Arrah, Bihar, whose deity is regarded as the guardian of the city and from whom the town is said to take its name. Tradition links it to the Mahabharata era and to Rama's journey. The old building was being replaced by a new multi-storey one as of 2022.","etiquette_notes":null,"native_name":null,"morning_opens_at":null,"morning_closes_at":null,"evening_opens_at":null,"eve